# Cursor Repo Rules (applies to all AI actions)

## Scope & Safety
- Never add real secrets (API keys, tokens, emails). Use placeholders and `.env.example`.
- Do not change encryption/security code unless explicitly asked and tested.
- Keep parsing logic deterministic with tests. No non-deterministic randomness in parsers.

## Code Quality
- Python: type hints required, docstrings for public functions, 100% lint clean.
- Testing: add/extend pytest for any new code. Provide a failing test FIRST when fixing a bug.
- Database: use Alembic migrations; never modify tables without a migration script.

## Architecture
- Keep modules small and focused: parsers/, models/, services/, api/.
- Do not add new external dependencies without approval & rationale in PR description.
- Prefer pure functions in parsers; no I/O inside parsing helpers.

## Commit & PR
- Use conventional commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, refactor:, test:, docs:.
- Always include a summary of what changed, why, and how it was tested.
- Large changes MUST be split into small PRs (max ~500 lines diff).

## Prompts (patterns)
- When asked to change code, show a short plan first (bullets) then propose the diff.
- When unsure, ask focused questions with 2–3 crisp options and a default recommendation.

## Non-Goals
- Do not wire external services (Kafka, Airflow, vLLM) unless the task requires it.
- Do not add UI frameworks beyond Next.js + Plotly for MVP.
